From 45319fab33ad1f3e6ed134825249051e8695fd58 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gaurav Sharma <mgsharm@amazon.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Nov 2025 03:39:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] amd-dkms: Disable drm_get_panel_min_brightness_quirk
 configure test

The drm_get_panel_min_brightness_quirk function exists in kernel 6.12 source
but lacks EXPORT_SYMBOL, making it unavailable to out-of-tree modules.
AMD DKMS autoconf incorrectly detects the function as available, causing
undefined symbol errors during module loading.

This patch comments out the configure script line that defines
HAVE_DRM_GET_PANEL_MIN_BRIGHTNESS_QUIRK, preventing the AMD driver
from attempting to use this unexported kernel function.

Fixes module loading errors for amdgpu.ko on kernel 6.12 when built
as out-of-tree DKMS module for MI355x GPU support.

Signed-off-by: Gaurav Sharma <mgsharm@amazon.com>
---
 amd/dkms/configure | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/amd/dkms/configure b/amd/dkms/configure
index 0c166c5..12b7aba 100755
--- a/amd/dkms/configure
+++ b/amd/dkms/configure
@@ -53497,7 +53497,7 @@ fi
 		else :
 
 
-printf "%s\n" "#define HAVE_DRM_GET_PANEL_MIN_BRIGHTNESS_QUIRK 1" >>confdefs.h
+# printf "%s\n" "#define HAVE_DRM_GET_PANEL_MIN_BRIGHTNESS_QUIRK 1" >>confdefs.h
 
 
 		fi
-- 
